  "overview": "<p><strong>IMPORTANT - ADDITIONAL PROGRAM REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Students must have a Tepitech score of at least 785 at the moment of the International Jury in order to be eligible for this destination</p><p><br></p><p>______________________________________________________________________________________</p><p><br></p><p><strong>VSB TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF OSTRAVA</strong></p><p><strong>VSB–Technicka Univerzita Ostrava</strong> (or <strong>Technical University of Ostrava</strong>) is one of the <strong>main engineering schools in the Czech Republic today</strong>.</p><ul><li>It has created its own <strong>business incubator</strong> that can bring together up to <strong>35 start-ups</strong> with a <strong>technology transfer center</strong>.</li><li>It also has an <strong>IT4Innovations</strong> pole.</li></ul><p><strong>Ostrava</strong> is the <strong>third largest city in the Czech Republic</strong>, with a population of <strong>over 300,000</strong>.</p><p>It is a <strong>multicultural, active city</strong> and has <strong>many events throughout the year</strong>.</p><p>For travel advice issued by the <strong>Ministry of Europe and Foreign Affairs</strong> on the <strong>Czech Republic</strong>, click <a href=\"https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/conseils-aux-voyageurs/conseils-par-pays-destination/republique-tcheque/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here.</a></p>",
  "administrative": "<p><strong>Application Dossier</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Once the IAFF office has sent your nomination, the <strong>partner university will contact you directly by email</strong> to start your application.</p><p>All required documents will have to be <strong>uploaded on their platform or sent by email</strong> before the deadline (see <strong>EMEA Teams channel</strong> for each application deadline).</p><p>If you have not received anything yet, it means your <strong>nomination has not been sent yet</strong>, please be patient.</p><p>To be completed with your <strong>Epitech bachelor campus administration</strong> during the <strong>registration period for Tech4</strong> (usually in April/May):</p><ul><li>The addendum to the contract.</li><li>EPITECH re-registration dossier.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Visa</p><ul><li>For <strong>European students</strong>, a <strong>valid passport/ national ID card</strong> is sufficient to travel to Europe (<strong>exception for the UK</strong>).</li><li>For <strong>non-Europeans students</strong> or students with a <strong>non-European citizenship</strong>, please check the <strong>immigration office of the host country</strong> to check the visa process and fees.</li></ul><blockquote>Students in France can use this website:</blockquote><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/</a></blockquote><p><br></p><p>Insurance</p><p>For European Students</p><p>The <strong>European Health Insurance Card (CEAM in French)</strong> is <strong>nominative and individual</strong>.</p><p>This card certifies your rights to the Health Insurance in Europe.</p><ul><li>To obtain your card, log in to your <strong>Ameli account</strong> at least <strong>two months before your departure</strong></li><li>It is <strong>free of charge</strong> and will be <strong>sent to your place within two weeks</strong></li><li>You can also <strong>download it online</strong></li></ul><blockquote><br></blockquote><blockquote>For more information:</blockquote><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.ameli.fr/assure/droits-demarches/europe-international/protection-sociale-etranger/etudes-etranger\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ameli.fr/assure/droits-demarches/europe-international/protection-sociale-etranger/etudes-etranger</a></blockquote><p><br></p><p>For Non-European Students</p><p>You must <strong>register for a private health insurance</strong> to cover your full stay.</p><p>Please check with your <strong>parents, bank, or any private insurance company</strong> for more information depending on the wanted coverage.</p><p>Ariane Registration (French Citizens Only)</p><p>Please register via the <strong>Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Ariane)</strong> platform to be aware of any news (<strong>terrorist attack, tsunami, earthquake…</strong>) in your host country:</p><p><a href=\"https://pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fildariane/dyn/public/login.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fildariane/dyn/public/login.html</a></p><p><br></p><p>Campus Life</p><p>The <strong>city of Ostrava</strong> is a <strong>residential city</strong> with more than <strong>300,000 inhabitants</strong>.</p><p>Ostrava is the <strong>third largest city in the Czech Republic</strong>, located <strong>10 km from the border with Poland</strong> and <strong>50 km from the border with Slovakia</strong>.</p><p>Once an <strong>industrial city</strong>, today it is an <strong>important business center</strong> of <strong>North Moravia and Silesia</strong>.</p><p>The city has <strong>three universities</strong> and is also a <strong>cultural hub</strong> with:</p><ul><li>Four theaters</li><li>Many galleries</li><li>Famous for holding <strong>concerts</strong>, <strong>festivals</strong>, and <strong>sporting events</strong></li></ul>",
  "accomodation": "<p>The city of Ostrava is a residential city with more than 300,000 inhabitants.</p><p>Ostrava is the third largest city in the Czech Republic, located 10 km from the border with Poland and 50 km from the border with Slovakia.</p><p>Once an industrial city, today it is an important business center of North Moravia and Silesia.</p><p>The city has three universities and is also a cultural hub with four theaters, many galleries and is famous for holding concerts, festivals and sporting events.</p>",
  "courses": "<p>Academic Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>You must validate <strong>30 ECTS credits per semester</strong>, i.e. <strong>60 over the year</strong>.</p><p>Semester Dates</p><ul><li>From the <strong>beginning of September to February</strong> of the following year</li><li>From the <strong>end of February to the beginning of July</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Faculty and Language of Instruction</p><p>You will study within the <strong>Faculty of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science</strong>.</p><p>Courses will be taught in <strong>English</strong> (<strong>level B1 recommended</strong>).</p><p>Some courses may require <strong>knowledge of mathematics</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>Course Selection</p><ul><li>You must validate <strong>60 credits over two semesters</strong></li><li>The <strong>Safety in Electrical Engineering course</strong> is <strong>compulsory</strong> (course code begins with <strong>410</strong>)</li><li>You can choose any course with a course code beginning with <strong>460</strong></li><li>You may also take <strong>Czech courses</strong> with codes beginning with <strong>712</strong></li></ul><blockquote>All eligible courses can be found on the following site:</blockquote><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vsb.cz/en/study/exchange-students/erasmus-plus/courses/fei/￼Note\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.vsb.cz/en/study/exchange-students/erasmus-plus/courses/fei/</a></blockquote><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vsb.cz/en/study/exchange-students/erasmus-plus/courses/fei/￼Note\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Note</strong></a>: You will only have access to the courses whose code begins with <strong>460</strong></blockquote><p><br></p><p>Course Format and Attendance</p><ul><li><strong>Each course is divided into two parts</strong>: a <strong>lecture part</strong> and a <strong>seminar part</strong></li><li><strong>Attendance of the seminar part is compulsory</strong></li><li>All courses are <strong>face-to-face</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>Course Structure and Assessment</p><ul><li>Teaching is <strong>fairly theoretical</strong>, with an obligation to read <strong>reference books</strong></li><li>There is a <strong>practical part</strong> involving <strong>exercises and practicals</strong></li><li><strong>A good level in mathematics</strong> is recommended</li></ul><p>Each subject:</p><ul><li>Has an <strong>overall mark out of 100</strong></li><li>The <strong>type of assessment</strong> is chosen by each teacher (exercises, projects, theory exams)</li><li>The <strong>exam period</strong> is scheduled, but each teacher can choose to place the exam <strong>outside the exam period</strong></li><li>Teachers may <strong>withdraw you from a subject</strong> if you miss too many seminars or fail key evaluations</li></ul><p>To register for an exam:</p><ul><li>You need to log in to the <strong>Edison website</strong>, access details are provided at the <strong>beginning of the year</strong></li></ul><p>EIP</p><p><strong>EIP</strong>: Any <strong>tech4 abroad</strong> involves an EIP!</p><p>Take advantage of the <strong>free slots</strong> you will have to <strong>advance them</strong>.</p>",
  "cost": "<p>Estimated Budget</p><p><br></p><p>The local currency is the <strong>Czech crown</strong> – <strong>„koruna“ (Kč, CZK)</strong>.</p><p><strong>1 Kč = 0.04 euros</strong> (rate September 2018)</p><ul><li><strong>Insurance</strong>: European insurance card \"Améli\" (<strong>free</strong>).</li><li>Apply for it at least <strong>1 month in advance</strong>.</li><li><strong>Housing</strong>: For a shared apartment (2 to 3 bedrooms), count <strong>500 to 800 €</strong></li><li>For expenses related to <strong>food, accommodation, and transport</strong>, students need around <strong>250 to 300 euros</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Sample Prices</strong></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p><br></p>",
